{
	"nodes":[
		{
			"id":"db891a56fd5d9f28",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# What is Excel?\n\n- IDE\n- Functional programing environment\n- Standard way to exchange data\n",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-640,
			"y":-440,
			"width":520,
			"height":340,
			"color":"3"
		},
		{
			"id":"98407dd6e56c0f6f",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Who invented spreadsheets?\n\nIn 1979, the two students invented **VisiCalc** after getting frustrated with homework in a business class, which led them to develop a radically new solution.\n\nOn the link below you can try the original VisiCalc online in an emulator. Note that the system RAM was only 64 KB :) \n\nhttps://www.pcjs.org/software/pcx86/app/other/visicalc/1981/\n\n\n",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-640,
			"y":-60,
			"width":520,
			"height":340,
			"color":"3"
		},
		{
			"id":"29d06c7d0474467b",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Why excel? \n\n- In 1982 Lotus 1-2-3, an electronic spreadsheet that became the best-selling personal-computer software of its day. \n- Microsoft Excel was first released in **1985**, initially for the Apple Macintosh. The Windows version followed in **1987**.\n- VBA (Visual Basic for Applications) was added to Excel in **1993**, with the release of **Excel 5.0**. ",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-640,
			"y":320,
			"width":520,
			"height":340,
			"color":"3"
		},
		{
			"id":"3ec72cb6e4a932ce",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# What happened to VisiCalc? \n\nMeanwhile, Lotus 1-2-3 appeared and quickly took over VisiCalc's market position. In 1985, Lotus Development Corporation acquired Software Arts (and with it, the rights to VisiCalc), and almost immediately pulled the product from the market, since it would have competed with its own Lotus 1-2-3 software.\n\nQ: Could the idea have been protected by a patent? ",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-80,
			"y":-60,
			"width":520,
			"height":340,
			"color":"5"
		},
		{"id":"682caac29248e14d","type":"file","file":"BDA/Lecture notes/_Build your professional reputation.md","x":480,"y":320,"width":520,"height":340,"color":"5"},
		{
			"id":"ad7fbb901bdedb11",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Joel Spolsky\n\nhttps://www.joelonsoftware.com/",
			"styleAttributes":{},
